    "narrative": "The standout play for LawDog today is **Lawrence Butler**, who leads our starting lineup with a strong 73.95 rating. His matchup against Kumar Rocker is highly favorable, bolstered by a 10% park factor boost and a significant 13% dynamic platoon edge against the right-handed arm. **Jonathan Aranda** also projects as a high-floor start (68.94) against Bassitt; his value is heavily inflated by a massive 19% SP skill advantage and a 12% platoon boost, making him a prime candidate to anchor our offensive production. While **Gleyber Torres** and **Brendan Donovan** sit just inside the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold, both benefit from favorable lineup spots and platoon alignments that keep them firmly in the starting mix.\n\nRegarding our bench decisions, **Braden Montgomery** was the most difficult exclusion, finishing at a 39.17 rating\u2014just shy of our 40.0 floor. While he receives a slight park bump, the 17% drag from the opposing pitcher, Jobe, ultimately relegated him to the bench to preserve our game caps. Elsewhere, we are exercising caution with **Cal Raleigh**, **Zack Gelof**, **Brendan Donovan**, and **Jung Hoo Lee**, as their lineups remain pending. Should those projections shift significantly upon official release, we will monitor their scores, particularly for **Jung Hoo Lee**, whose score is currently buoyed by a 5% wind-out factor that could evaporate if weather conditions shift. **Gavin Sheets** remains our most volatile start; he sits right at the bottom of the marginal tier (40.12) due to a challenging matchup against Williams, and we will monitor his performance closely to ensure he does not become a drain on our efficiency metrics.",
